lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We are now close to building YP =
3.3 rc1 for the final release. That build may happen later today if =
three are no more urgent pending changes. The biggest blockers on =
release may be the changelog/release notes and migration guide as those =
have not been started yet.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l4 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.2.3 was =
released.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l4 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We did merge a change to =
oeqa/runqemu to allow the qemu images to be run from a tmpfs. This =
should mean writes aren&#8217;t held up in the IO queue which we believe =
may have been a cause of the intermittent failures. Unfortunately we =
can&#8217;t use cgroups as the versions on most of the autobuilder =
workers isn&#8217;t recent enough for IO priorities, even ignoring the =
permission issues so this tmpfs solution seemed like the best option and =
was not very invasive to implement. It does mean we now see the =
&#8220;qemu didn&#8217;t start in 120s&#8221; error instead much more =
regularly if the copy into tmpfs is locked.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l4 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are a number of patches =
queued in master-next but most are version upgrades which will wait for =
3.4 to open for development.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l4 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent autobuilder issues =
continue to occur and are now at a record high level. You&nbsp; can see =
the list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
style=3D'mso-margin-top-alt:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin=
-left:.5in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>We are working to =
identify the load pattern on the infrastructure that seems to trigger =
these.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p =
style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
